pe":"Question","name":"How Often Do Tires Need Rotated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Tire rotation is a routine maintenance service that should be performed every 3,000 to 6,000 miles."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Included with a Tire Rotation Service?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"First, our tire technicians will carefully evaluate the position of your tires and the wear they’ve sustained to determine if it’s time for a rotation.If, based on our recommendation, you decide on a rotation, our next step will be to help preserve the life of your tires with a service that includes: Removing your tires Carefully inspecting their tread-wear patterns Rotating your tires to the positions recommended by your vehicle manufacturer Resetting your tire-pressure monitoring system (TPMS) as neededLearn more about our Tire Pressure Monitoring System Service and when you may need it."}}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org/","@type":"WebSite","url":"index.html","potentialAction":{"@type":"SearchAction","target":{"@type":"EntryPoint","urlTemplate":"index.html?q={search_term_string"},"query-input":"required name=search_term_string"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org/","@type":"Service","name":"Tire Rotation","brand":{"@type":"Brand","name":"Goodyear"},"description":"Do you feel your tires are wearing differently and causing issues while driving? You may need to rotate your tires. Bring your vehicle in to one of our locations today and we will inspect your tire’s wear patterns then rotate your tires as needed.","url":"-us/services/tire-rotation_211145/index.html","provider":{"@type":"LocalBusiness","name":"Goodyear"}}</script><!--$--><!--$--><!--/$--><div class="Services relative min-h-screen"><!--$--><!--/$--><div><div class="opacity-100"><div class="analytics-event-listener contents"></div></div><nav role="navigation" aria-label="Jump Navigation" class="w-full shado